ged hardcoded model string `'claude-opus-5-5'` to use SDK constants (`Model::CLAUDE_OPUS_5_5` in PHP, `Anthropic::Model::CLAUDE_OPUS_5_5` in Ruby). This is a best practice change for SDK usage.\n\n2. **search-results.md**: \n   - Removed \"Always on\" language, simplified to just describe usage\n   - Removed the paragraph about all active models supporting search results (except Haiku 3) and no beta header needed\n   - Removed the limitation about search results being available on Claude API, Bedrock, and Google Cloud\n   - Changed \"Availability: Always on\" to \"Availability: Available\" for both Messages API and Managed Agents\n\n3. **effort.md**: Similar to search-results.md, removed \"Always on\" prefix from both Messages API and Managed Agents descriptions. Simplified the availability language.\n\n4. **claude-on-vertex-ai.md**: Changed the feature overview description from saying it \"lists every feature and whether Claude Models on Google Cloud supports it\" to \"lists every feature. Each feature's page shows whether Claude Models on Google Cloud supports it.\" - moving the support info from the overview page to individual feature pages.\n\nKey themes:\n- SDK best practices: using constants instead of hardcoded strings\n- Availability language standardization: \"Always on\" \u2192 \"Available\"\n- Documentation restructuring: moving support details to per-feature pages\n- Removing overly broad availability claims (removing blanket \"all models support\" statements and platform availability from limitations)"}, {"timestamp": "20:49 EST", "sources": [{"id": "claude-code", "name": "Claude Code", "pages": [{"slug": "amazon-bedrock", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+3 lines, -3 lines", "added": 3, "removed": 3, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "cli-reference", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+1 lines, -1 lines", "added": 1, "removed": 1, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "desktop", "source_id": "clau